//~ compile_fail(backend)
//~ error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch

// NEGATIVE (must FAIL to compile): open a 9P connection and close it without
// ever speaking on it. This is pillar 4's asymmetry for `uk9p`, at the outer
// level of the nesting.
//
// `disconnect` accepts only <!drained>, and <drained!> is minted only by
// `session.end` — reachable only through `attach`, which is reachable only
// through `version` — or by the named escape `session.skipped`. So a device
// that was connected and then immediately thrown away has no way out.
//
// WHAT THE C DOES INSTEAD: nothing, correctly and silently. `uk_9pdev_connect`
// followed by `uk_9pdev_disconnect` is a well-formed pair — the assertion at
// 9pdev.c:265 is satisfied, `_fid_mgmt_cleanup` finds an empty active list, and
// the transport's disconnect runs. It is not a memory error. It is a DESIGN
// error, and an expensive one on this particular resource: a 9P connect is a
// virtqueue setup and a device negotiation against a host daemon, so a mount
// nobody uses is a host-side file descriptor, a QEMU thread and a virtqueue
// held for the life of the unikernel.
//
// The legitimate case stays expressible and stays loud: `boot_session.kz`'s
// second flow says `unikraft/ninep:session.skipped` and boots. What this
// rejects is the SILENT version, where "we changed our mind about this mount"
// and "somebody forgot to attach" are spelled identically.
//
//     grep -r "ninep:session.skipped"   ->   "which mounts do we open and
//                                             never attach to"
//
// EXPECTED: error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch: expected
//           'unikraft.ninep:drained' but got 'unikraft.ninep:linked!'
//           for argument 'dev'

// The `unikraft` namespace is declared here, not inherited: koruc's built-in
// alias probes the sibling koru-libs CHECKOUT, so in a worktree this file would
// otherwise compile against main's lifts instead of the ones beside it.
~std/compiler:paths {
    unikraft: {{ ENTRY }}/../..
}

~import unikraft/ninep
~import std/io

~unikraft/ninep:connect(tag: "korufs")
| ok mount |> unikraft/ninep:disconnect(dev: mount): rc
    |> std/io:print.ln("should never get here: {{ rc:d }}")
| absent why |> std/io:print.ln("connect: {{ why:s }}")
| refused e |> std/io:print.ln("connect: {{ e.reason:s }} ({{ e.errno:d }})")
